  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find ${A}^{2}.$\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\">${A}^{2}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-3}}\n</td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-4}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
  "worked_solution": "To find ${A}^{2},$ we multiply $A$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
